<core:FragmentDefinition
  xmlns:core="sap.ui.core"
  xmlns:macros="sap.fe.macros">
  <!--
    Issue #426 — the "Task" cell in the Path Items LineItem table needs a
    value help that differs by row type: TUTORIAL → Tutorials picker,
    GROUP → Groups picker, CHECKPOINT → free-text checkpoint title.

    History of failed fixes (do NOT reintroduce a hand-rolled Input):
      #1331 eager-loaded the core:require handler in Component.js;
      #1345 added targetType:'any' to a showValueHelp expression binding.
    Both were correct in isolation yet the F4 icon stayed missing on the
    DEPLOYED approuter. Root cause (verified 2026-07-27 via Playwright on DEV +
    a faithful local hybrid repro): admin child components ship WITHOUT a
    Component-preload.js. On the deployed shell (which HAS a root preload,
    optimized async mode) the runtime requests components/missions/
    Component-preload.js, gets a non-executable HTML fallback, and the
    core:require handler resolves LATER than Fiori Elements' synchronous
    column-template clone. With `handler` unresolved at clone time the
    showValueHelp expression binding silently degrades to a bare path binding
    on the String `taskType`, which UI5 coerces to Boolean → FormatException
    ("TUTORIAL is not a valid boolean value") → showValueHelp:false → no icon.
    This only reproduces under deployed load-timing, which is why the earlier
    fixes passed local/standalone checks but failed on DEV.

    Fix: drop the core:require handler + expression binding entirely and use
    native sap.fe.macros:Field building blocks — the SAME pattern the sibling
    TypeColumn.fragment.xml already uses successfully on DEV. Each Field binds
    its own metaPath and FE renders that field's value help natively from the
    existing @Common.ValueList annotations on AdminService.CompletionPathItems
    (tutorial_ID → Tutorials, group_ID → Groups; see app/admin-annotations.cds).
    There is no lazily-loaded module to lose a race against and no expression
    binding over a Boolean property to coerce, so the failure mode is removed
    by construction.

    Per-type visibility uses the server-computed Boolean fields
    show{Tutorial,Group,Checkpoint} (srv/admin-service.cds — `case when
    taskType = '…'`). These are genuine Booleans in the model, so binding them
    to macros:Field `visible` needs no expression and no coercion. Exactly one
    is true per row, so exactly one Field renders in the cell.
  -->
  <macros:Field
    metaPath="tutorial_ID"
    visible="{showTutorial}"/>
  <macros:Field
    metaPath="group_ID"
    visible="{showGroup}"/>
  <macros:Field
    metaPath="checkpointTitle"
    visible="{showCheckpoint}"/>
</core:FragmentDefinition>
